31. Match the concept with its definition:\par
Items:\par
1. Fencing\par
2. Quorum\par
3. LXC\par
4. Snapshot\par
5. Live Migration\par
\par
Definitions:\par
A. Moving a running VM between nodes without downtime.\par
B. Majority vote required for cluster operations.\par
C. Isolating or rebooting a failed node to protect data.\par
D. Linux-based OS-level virtualization (containers).\par
E. Saving the current state of a disk and RAM.\par
\par
\b Answer:\b0\par
1-C, 2-B, 3-D, 4-E, 5-A\par
